n it off?  well.. get that snazzy thingy I mentioned above 'Set Herms' and turn off the "CHECK LOGON" check box.  You can mess around w/ all those but be warned I don't know what the side effects would be! (most likely nothing major, I hope) ¥	I found a bug not in the list!  HELP!   E-Mail me, I will be available until August of 1996, after that I will be leaving on a LDS mission for 2 years & you most likely won't be able to get in touch w/ me.  You should include what the error is (numeric error code if one is given), details about when it happens, what other externals you are running, what system version, what hermes version, and what type of computer you're running; if you include these things I will be more likely to get the bug fixed.Internet:  ddolinar@utw.comOlympus: "Dave Dolinar" my BBS:   (801)756-6417   I'm the Sysop.Updating: (yipee!)	Slycrel Dev v2.00 -> Slycrel Dev v2.01		1- Remove the old Slycrel External from the Externals Folder.		2- Drop new Slycrel External into the Externals Folder.	Version BEFORE Dev v2.00		1- Follow the "general installation" instructions.General Installation: (skippy!)1- Unstuff the file (duh, you most likely already have if you're reading this!)2- Delete any old Slycrel Files you have in your Externals folder, this includes all the slycrel folders & everything.3- Drag the "G>[0;34mSlycrel[12C" external and the "Sly_Data" folder into your Externals folder.4- Add about 300k to your Hermes Memory, you can do this in the 'get info' box.5- Run Hermes6- Logon & enter the realm.7- Make a character, you can edit all sorts of stuff, keep re-rolling until you're satisified w/ the character.  (we intend on making this new-character generation a little smother & easier to follow)8- Enter the Town & play...Things for the Future:Æ	Addition of Smart Monsters that actually SHOOT and manuver w/ a little stratagie.Æ	Addition of the Guilds so that the uesrs can go up in levels.Æ	NPC (non-playing-characters) that yo